  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Project Website**\n\nI\'m focusing on defining the website\'s core structure for the LODissea project. The initial aim is to create a website exploring the Europeana database for six different countries. I\'m starting with the opening section, envisioning a hero section with a paper boat icon and the title \"LODissea\".\n\n\n**Structuring the UI elements**\n\nI\'m now outlining the second section, the \"About\" section, with a blue sea background. I\'m planning out the necessary text content for this section, including project details, team information, and a disclaimer for credits. I\'m also planning the Journey Map section with an interactive European map focused on the six chosen countries and animating the paper boat. I\'ve decided to build the website as a client-side SPA using React/Vite with Tailwind for styling. I plan to use animations with `motion/react` and icons with `lucide-react`, potentially using the `Sailboat` icon, or creating a custom SVG if needed.\n\n\n**Designing the Component Architecture**\n\nI\'m now diving into the component architecture. I\'ve decided on the key components: `App.tsx` for layout and scrolling, a Navbar, a Hero section, an About section (project details, team, and credits), and the interactive Map section. The map\'s styling will be crucial; I\'m leaning toward a stylized SVG or simplified conceptual representation using Tailwind, although I\'m considering using an existing Europe SVG, or `react-simple-maps`, depending on complexity. It needs to be quick. The whole structure aims for a single-page scrolling experience, driven by anchor links.\n\n\n**Refining the Map Implementation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the interactive map section. While initially considering static SVGs and styled React components, I\'ve decided to prioritize a simplified approach and quickly implement a map. I\'m leaning toward using `react-simple-maps` with `topojson` data. I\'ve found a suitable topojson file and will be installing the necessary dependencies. I will quickly look at implementing the base UI first and abstract it creatively, or switch to an SVG later if needed. The aim is a fast, visually engaging map. I\'ve also decided to create a custom SVG. I plan to use this for the base UI first.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 537303885
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
