  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visual Flow**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how to make the visual flow feel natural. I\'m prioritizing the movement of the boat, determining its ideal placement in the hero section and map journey text. My concern is making the \"journey begins\" text move from the bottom-left of the sea to the middle-left.\n\n\n**Refining Movement and Visuals**\n\nI\'ve made some adjustments. I\'ve removed the vertical page numbers and status indicators from the hero section. The boat\'s starting position is now top, and I\'m ensuring it fits the new flow. The \"Journey Begins\" text has moved to the middle-left. The boat animation is undergoing adjustments to align with the text, particularly the \"toLeft\" phase. \"QQ1\" has also been removed. The progress line integration is now a focus, and I need to start it from either the map or analysis section.\n\n\n**Connecting Progress Line**\n\nI\'m now focused on the progress line\'s integration. Instead of making it connect seamlessly to the analysis section, I\'ll extend it upwards to align with the boat\'s endpoint in the map journey. I\'ve adjusted the boat\'s \"toLeft\" phase to remove \"QQ1\" and keep the progress line on the left. The `MapJourney` text is also changed to be centered vertically. Additionally, the hero section has lost its line components.\n\n\n**Adjusting Boat Coordinates**\n\nI\'m now refining the boat\'s coordinates, particularly for the \"toLeft\" phase. The objective is to make the boat align precisely with the \"Journey Begins\" text, ensuring the text is at `left-32` while positioning the boat at approximately `left-40px` and `top-1/2`. The progress line\'s start will be drawn in `MapJourney` when the boat is \"toLeft.\" I also removed \"QQ1\" from the `AnalysisSection` component. The boat\'s movement is undergoing optimization to work with absolute coordinates.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Transitions**\n\nI\'m now reconsidering the boat\'s movement in light of scaling issues and the desired user experience. Instead of trying to precisely map SVG coordinates to DOM pixels, I\'m exploring solutions that involve the boat staying within the SVG or accepting a small visual jump. I\'m focusing on making the boat transition from the title\'s top to the front of the NL text and then alongside \"journey begins\". I\'m also considering `Framer Motion`\'s layout animations. However, I\'ve decided to refine current simulation and enhance positions.\n\n\n**Aligning Coordinates and Text**\n\nI\'m now implementing the changes for aligning the text and boat. I\'ve updated the text div to be vertically centered and adjusted the boat\'s coordinates in `MapJourney.tsx` to match. The progress line is being introduced with an initial height animation. I\'ve modified the `top` values to center the title with the boat. Also the boat\'s initial phase is now complete.\n\n\n**Deleting Unnecessary Elements**\n\nI\'m removing the \"QQ1\" text as planned from both `MapJourney.tsx` and `AnalysisSection.tsx` components. My focus is on the boat\'s precise placement in relation to the text, and this will help streamline the design. The current positions now seem optimal.\n\n\n**Refining Final Animation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the final animation refinements, specifically addressing the scaling and flow concerns. I\'m focusing on the `MapJourney.tsx` file for the boat. My plan is to optimize the boat\'s \"toLeft\" phase to enhance the visual integration. I\'ve also re-examined the initial positioning, ensuring it feels natural and visually appealing for the user.\n\n\n**Optimizing Final Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the final animation. I\'m focusing on ensuring the visual flow is seamless. The adjustments to the \'toLeft\' phase now incorporate the boat\'s movement relative to the left side and center of the screen, enhancing user experience. I removed \'QQ1\'. The goal is to create a dynamic and appealing visual narrative.\n\n\n**Finalizing Layout and Animation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on finalizing the layout and animation elements in the `MapJourney.tsx` file. The goal is a visually appealing and dynamic user experience. The text positioning, especially its vertical alignment, is being carefully reviewed. I am also working to ensure the boat\'s \"toLeft\" phase and the progress line integrate seamlessly.\n\n\n**Refining Text Placement**\n\nI\'m now implementing updates to the text placement. I\'m focusing on \"The Journey Begins\" text\'s styling within the hero section. I\'ve updated the text to center it, along with its description, using a new div. The position of the text\'s top, and its left position is being changed, and is now at `left-24 md:left-32`. I\'m removing \"QQ1\" from `AnalysisSection.tsx`, too, and fixing the line start. The goal is improving readability and user experience.\n\n\n**Adjusting Visual Transitions**\n\nI\'m now refining the boat\'s \"toLeft\" phase within the `AnalysisSection` component. I\'m adjusting its `boatY` animation to transition smoothly from `0vh` at the top of the section. The scaling and visual flow remain my primary focus, ensuring seamless integration between the `MapJourney` and `AnalysisSection`.\n\n\n**Revising Animation Transitions**\n\nI\'m now revising the animation transitions, specifically the boat\'s vertical movement. My goal is to ensure a cohesive visual experience between sections. I\'m focusing on the `AnalysisSection` component, adapting the `boatY` animation to transition smoothly from the top of the section. The boat in `AnalysisSection` is now set to start at `top: 0%` of its `h-screen`. After considering the text placement, I need to ensure that Hero, MapJourney, and AnalysisSection match perfectly. I\'m changing the `boatY` mapping to be `useTransform(scrollYProgress, [0, 1], [\"0vh\", \"80vh\"]);`.\n\n\n"
